## Oracle run report — 2026-08-20, run 2 (scope: BL-5)

**One decision landed: OD-4, resolving BL-5 by adopting the steward's proposed default as filed.** The R1000 steward plan delivers only the `.12g` formatting rule and its blind unit tests (including the ESC-1 reproduction, red-then-green); the S1 and S2 acceptance scripts are delivered by the milestone plans that build the command they invoke — S1 by `convert`, S2 by `temperature` — each carrying OD-1's exact-stdout constraint verbatim, and no acceptance script lands before its command exists. OD-1's "observable twice" clause is refined, not superseded; R1000 is unchanged, no criterion was waived, no halt was written.

**Why I was confident.** The gate itself settled it: `acceptance-criteria.sh` deliberately reports an unscripted criterion without failing ("failing the pipeline for it would stop the build that would make it pass"), while a landed failing script goes hard red on every subsequent PR — and a landed script can never be deleted while its criterion stands, so landing S1 early is a one-way door into a red pipeline. The only sequencing consistent with both the gate's design and OD-1's measurement obligation is the one BL-5 proposed. A consequence worth noting: the ESC-1 correction row in `docs/escapes.md` waits for the PR that lands `acceptance/S1.sh` (the `convert` milestone), so the stub stays visibly pending until then — accurately.

**Contradictions found but not decided:** none in scope. Two Proposed backlog items (unit aliases; sub-absolute-zero temperatures) remain unruled and were deliberately left out of the handoff's id-space so the driver doesn't mark them processed.

