**On the vision.** Nothing ambiguous this run, but the same gap recurs: this was the third decision (after OD-1's measurement clause and OD-4) that leaned on the unnumbered purpose statement or the durable-evidence prose because the numbered V1–V6 say nothing about *the pipeline itself staying alive* — e.g. "a required check that can only go red must not land before the work that turns it green." If the owner numbered a sentence to that effect, sequencing rulings like this one would cite it directly instead of deriving it from the purpose statement.
